RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
2026-07-30: Profiled the immutable evaluation mechanics, task-row distributions, exact label reconstruction, daily episode counts, overdispersion, and validation/test coldness. The required profile is stored at repository root because the caller marks every file under kapso_evaluation as immutable and declares any modification there to be evaluation tampering.
2026-07-30: Replaced the trivial baseline with a causal all-table threshold-process pipeline: exact daily episodes, multi-horizon intensity/funnel/cohort features, eight decayed signed CountSketch channels, direct/hurdle/count/mechanistic heads, negative-binomial assessment, purged forward OOF selection, and distinct Model-A/Model-B refits.
2026-07-30: The first debug run failed while filtering sketch events because nullable VisitStream/PhoneRequestsStream UserID values could not convert to int64. Invalid and null user rows are now removed before sketch indexing; the second debug run and prediction contract check passed.
2026-07-30: Full evaluation v1 completed in 785.8 seconds with 0.696193 validation ROC-AUC. Forward folds selected direct+hurdle+Poisson heads for Model A and rejected the mechanistic and negative-binomial additions.
2026-07-30: Widened the matrix with user identity, clicked position/HistCTR, price distribution, per-search click counts, daily bursts, and user-agent cohort CTR. Added fold-safe categorical handling for LightGBM and count-only/hurdle-only candidates to head inclusion selection.
2026-07-31: Full v2 categorical evaluation completed in 1,070.43 seconds with stronger internal Model-A meta mean (0.69742) but 0.694716 official validation ROC-AUC. The categorical direct and hurdle heads collapsed to roughly 0.58-0.66 fold AUC because sparse high-cardinality identifiers overfit; two debug ablations isolated categorical handling as the cause, so the identifiers remain ordinary numeric features and smoothed cohort statistics carry category information.
2026-07-31: Internal April-only ablations showed 700 count rounds beat 1,200 by 0.0051 mean and 0.0061 worst-fold ROC-AUC, and full core-plus-sketch features beat core-only by 0.0066 mean. A fixed three-seed Poisson ensemble improved every purged April fold over its first member by 0.00063, 0.00138, and 0.00246, so count predictions now average three independently seeded models.
